  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Determine the largest interval on which the function $f(x)=\\sqrt{18+3x}$ is continuous.",
  "worked_solution": "Our function is a radical function, so it is continuous over all points in its domain.\n\nTo find the domain of $\\sqrt{18+3x}$, we set the expression under the radical to be greater than or equal to zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}18+3x\\ge 0\\,\u27f9\\,3x\\ge -18\\,\u27f9\\, & \\,x\\ge -6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $f(x)$ is $[-6,\\infty )$, and the function is continuous on this interval.",
